    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d650">

                <pb facs="0814" n="704" xml:id="pg704"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3307: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-23T19:00:00+08:00">December 23, 1931—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 23—6:44 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1125. The Consul at Dairen reports on December 22, 4 p.m., as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Japanese military authorities there are commandeering auto trucks on an
                            extensive scale and shipping them northward.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>The Consul General at Mukden reports on December 22, 10 p.m., as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>That afternoon trucks loaded with boxes marked “shrapnel” were observed
                            en route to the railway. Taken in conjunction with the Dairen report
                            mentioned above, this would indicate that the anticipated drive by
                            Japanese troops westward is imminent.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
